{"name":"Au Clair de la Lune","hex":"#f4f2e2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lune","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fit of lunacy or madness; a period of frenzy; a crazy or unreasonable freak."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A concave figure formed by the intersection of the arcs of two circles on a plane, or on a sphere the intersection between two great semicircles.","Anything crescent-shaped."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lune"}],"entries":[{"title":"Au clair de la lune","blocks":[{"text":"\"Au clair de la lune\" is a French folk song of the 18th century. Its composer and lyricist are unknown. Its simple melody is commonly taught to beginners learning an instrument. In the history of sound recording, it has the distinction of being the first ever recorded music (1860)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Au_Clair_de_la_Lune_children%27s_book_2.jpg/330px-Au_Clair_de_la_Lune_children%27s_book_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Au_clair_de_la_lune","wikidata":"Q758389"},{"title":"Au clair de la lune (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Au clair de la lune is a Canadian drama film, directed by André Forcier and released in 1983. The film stars Guy L'Écuyer as Albert, a washed-up former bowling champion living in his car while dreaming of recapturing his past success, and Michel Côté as François, an albino who moves into the car after Bert saves his life."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Au_clair_de_la_lune_(film)","wikidata":"Q2870330"},{"title":"La Lune","blocks":[{"text":"La Lune was the name of a nineteenth-century French weekly four-sheet newspaper edited by Francis Polo. The illustrator André Gill became known for his work for this journal, in which he drew caricatures for a series entitled The Man of the Day."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Portrait_authentique_de_Rocambole%2C_Paris_Mus%C3%A9es_20231107131605.jpg/330px-Portrait_authentique_de_Rocambole%2C_Paris_Mus%C3%A9es_20231107131605.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Lune","wikidata":"Q1798913"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Ly_au_clair_de_la_lune_accords_melodie_paroles.png/500px-Ly_au_clair_de_la_lune_accords_melodie_paroles.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Ly_au_clair_de_la_lune_accords_melodie_paroles.png/500px-Ly_au_clair_de_la_lune_accords_melodie_paroles.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chords, melody and words\n\n\n\nMIDI rendition\n\n\n","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALy_au_clair_de_la_lune_accords_melodie_paroles.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Ang_mus_young.JPG/500px-Ang_mus_young.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Ang_mus_young.JPG/500px-Ang_mus_young.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Young et sa fille by Pierre-Auguste Vafflard (1804)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAng_mus_young.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Andr%C3%A9_Gill_%28autoportrait%29.jpg/120px-Andr%C3%A9_Gill_%28autoportrait%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Andr%C3%A9_Gill_%28autoportrait%29.jpg/250px-Andr%C3%A9_Gill_%28autoportrait%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Andr%C3%A9_Gill_%28autoportrait%29.jpg/120px-Andr%C3%A9_Gill_%28autop